{"step_index":76,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T17:30:16Z","input_tokens":2090,"cache_read_tokens":71597,"output_tokens":2641,"content":"# JanaSeva: Public Grievance & Civic Issue Reporting Portal\n### VTU 3rd Semester Community Project (Course Code: 1BCP308)\n\nWelcome to your project! As a beginner, you don't need to worry about complex setups or code errors. We have designed and built a complete web application tailored specifically for your **VTU 1BCP308 Community Project**, styled after the official Indian government civic portal in your reference image.\n\n---\n\n## 🌟 What We Built for You\n\nYour application includes all the features you requested, matching your design screenshot:\n\n1. **Official Indian Civic Portal Theme**:\n   - **Deep Navy Blue Header** (`#0f2444`) with Ashoka / Civic emblem placeholder, state portal banner, and live active status badge.\n   - **Hero Section**: *\"Serving Citizens with Transparency and Trust\"*, with call-to-action buttons (*\"Report Civic Problem\"* & *\"Track Existing Issue\"*) and a live Ward Control Room ticker card.\n2. **Civic Issue Reporting**:\n   - 6 Quick Categories: **Potholes & Roads**, **Garbage & Waste**, **Streetlights**, **Water Leaks**, **Drainage & Sewage**, and **Sanitation**.\n   - Input fields: Category, Short Title, Nearby Landmark/Area, Detailed Description, Urgency Level, and Resident Pseudonym.\n   - **Photo Upload**: Supports uploading any image from your computer or phone with instant preview, plus 1-click **demo preset photos** (pothole, garbage, streetlight) for smooth live presentations.\n   - Generates an auto-assigned tracking code (e.g., `TKT-8942`) and shows a success confirmation card.\n3. **Real-time Status Tracking**:\n   - Enter any ticket ID (or click realistic demo presets like `TKT-8941` or `TKT-8938`).\n   - 3-stage visual progress stepper: **Submitted ➔ In Progress ➔ Resolved**.\n   - Shows municipal inspection logs and ward officer action remarks.\n4. **Public Transparency Feed**:\n   - Filter complaints by status (**All**, **Submitted**, **In Progress**, **Resolved**) or category.\n   - Shows issue cards with attached evidence and timestamps.\n5. **Privacy Protection**:\n   - Does **not** ask for or expose any personal phone numbers or exact door addresses. Only public landmarks (e.g., *\"Near College Main Gate\"*) are used.\n6. **VTU 1BCP308 Academic Section**:\n   - Built-in tab explaining the Problem Statement, Proposed Solution, and alignment with **UN SDG 11** (*Sustainable Cities and Communities*) & **SDG 16** (*Strong Institutions*).\n   - Includes a **\"Print Project Report Card\"** button for your project dossier.\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 How to Run and Present Your Project\n\nWe have provided **two ways** to run your project:\n\n### Method 1: Instant 1-Click Browser Demo (Zero Setup Required)\nIf you need to test the website right now or show it to your guide or friends without installing software:\n\n1. Open **File Explorer** on your computer.\n2. Paste this path into the File Explorer address bar and press **Enter**:\n   ```text\n   C:\\Users\\pinkm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\a5b231a2-4f86-4de8-aef6-e2920d9db8fb\n   ```\n3. Look for the file named **`civic_portal.html`**.\n4. Double-click it (or right-click and choose **Open with > Google Chrome** or **Microsoft Edge**).\n5. The complete, interactive portal will open in your browser! You can file complaints, upload photos, track tickets, and filter the public feed.\n\n---\n\n### Method 2: Running with React + Vite.js (For Full Viva Inspection)\nAll modular React and Vite source files have been generated in:\n```text\nC:\\Users\\pinkm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\a5b231a2-4f86-4de8-aef6-e2920d9db8fb\\react-vite-project\\\n```\n\n#### File Structure:\n```text\nreact-vite-project/\n├── package.json              # Project dependencies (React 18, Vite, Tailwind)\n├── vite.config.js            # Vite configuration\n├── tailwind.config.js        # Civic portal color schemes\n├── index.html                # Entry HTML\n├── src/\n│   ├── main.jsx              # React DOM mounting\n│   ├── App.jsx               # Main state & view controller\n│   ├── index.css             # Tailwind imports\n│   ├── data/\n│   │   └── sampleIssues.js   # Indian college-town realistic sample data\n│   └── components/\n│       ├── Header.jsx        # Navigation & Gov banner\n│       ├── Hero.jsx          # \"Serving Citizens with Transparency\" banner\n│       ├── ServicesGrid.jsx  # 6 civic categories & live stats\n│       ├── ReportIssueForm.jsx # Grievance filing form with photo upload\n│       ├── TrackIssue.jsx    # Progress stepper & ticket lookup\n│       ├── IssuesFeed.jsx    # Filterable transparency board\n│       ├── VtuProjectSection.jsx # 1BCP308 syllabus documentation\n│       └── Footer.jsx        # Civic portal footer\n└── README.md                 # Project summary and viva cheat-sheet\n```\n\n#### How to run it:\n1. **Install Node.js**:\n   - Download the LTS version from [nodejs.org](https://nodejs.org/) and run the installer (click \"Next\" until complete).\n2. **Copy the folder to your Documents or Desktop**:\n   - Copy the `react-vite-project` folder to your `Documents` or `Desktop` folder (e.g., `C:\\Users\\pinkm\\Documents\\civic-issue-portal`).\n   *(Tip for beginners: Windows protects the root `C:\\` drive by default, which is why keeping your coding projects in `Documents` or `Desktop` avoids Windows permission prompts).*\n3. **Start the Vite development server**:\n   - Open Command Prompt or PowerShell, navigate to your folder, and run:\n     ```bash\n     npm install\n     npm run dev\n     ```\n   - Open the URL shown on your screen (typically `http://localhost:5173`) in your browser.\n\n---\n\n## 🎓 VTU 1BCP308 Viva Voce & Presentation Cheat-Sheet\n\nHere are typical questions your project guide or external evaluator might ask, along with answers:\n\n| Question | Recommended Answ